{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Every Tinker build pet dies when its health runs out (#1411)",
  "contract": "#1411 reports a Tinker pet that stayed alive at 0 health, without naming the pet or the damage. A pet whose health is exhausted must die like any creature: Unit::DealDamage kills a victim when the damage reaches its health, and Pet::Update removes a dead summoned pet (only hunter pets keep a corpse), so the owner loses it. The Tinker builds are SPELL_EFFECT_SUMMON_PET spells for the five permanent pets that npc_ascension_tinker_pet rescales every second: Build: Scrapmaw 500242 (50048), Build: ZIGGI-6K 524840 (500481), Build: Mechano-Bear 803405 (60671), Build: Clockwork Assistant 803436 (60070) and Build: Rusthound 803437 (60672). Each pet is set to 1 health beside its Tinker and hit by Decoy Explosive 53273 cast by a golem 3 yd away (10 yd around the golem, SPELL_ATTR3_ALWAYS_HIT, 1440 to 2160 Physical), so the blow always lands and is lethal; the Tinker's health is raised as a fixture so the same blast cannot kill it. A pet that survived at 0 health would still be reported by pet_entry.",
  "timeout_ms": 180000,
